    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=## Objective\n\nResearch this company and return their key contacts for Dream 100 outreach. The goal is to identify the decision makers who would receive and act on a cold outreach package — specifically, who owns pipeline at this company.\n\nCompany Name: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Name }}\nWebsite: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Website }}\n\n---\n\nFind THREE CONTACTS:\n\n### Contact 1 — PRIMARY (D100 Target)\n\nThe person the Dream 100 package is addressed to and sent to. They must own pipeline — the person who feels the pain of an empty calendar and has authority to say yes to a lead gen engagement.\n\nAt a founder-led company: Founder / CEO.\nAt a company with a dedicated sales team: VP Sales / Head of Sales / CRO.\n\n---\n\n### Contact 2 — SECONDARY\n\nSomeone who works directly alongside Primary on pipeline or growth. Co-Founder, Head of Growth, SDR Lead, or senior AE. Would be CC'd or forwarded to, not the main recipient.\n\n---\n\n### Contact 3 — FORWARDING\n\nANOTHER DECISION MAKER, if there is one.\n\nIf not, Someone who can pass this to the decision maker if we can't reach them directly. Not procurement, not legal. Could be an EA, Chief of Staff, or a junior sales person.\n\n(You can find more than one forwardable if relevant)\n\n---\n\n# Fields For Every Contact (do your best to fill as many as possible. Email and LinkedIn the most important)\n\n- Name:\n- Title:\n- Role: Primary / Secondary / Forwarding\n- LinkedIn:\n- Work Email:\n- Email Confidence: (high/medium/low + reason. Search Apollo first — if found, mark high. If pattern-based, mark medium or low)\n- Personal Email:\n- Phone:\n- Twitter/X:\n- Why included:\n\n---\n\n# RULES\n\n- Primary must be deliberate. Find the pipeline owner — do not default to a marketing role.\n- No procurement, legal, or finance unless clearly relevant.\n- If Primary cannot be confidently identified, state why.\n- For work email: identify the company email pattern from any publicly visible addresses, then apply it. Check press releases, GitHub commits, podcast show notes, conference speaker bios.\n- Search Apollo for every contact first — if found there, email is verified and confidence is high.\n- For personal email: search LinkedIn, personal websites, conference speaker pages, podcast appearances, Twitter/X bios.\n- No speculation. If unsure, state confidence level and reason.\n- DO NOT RETURN WITHOUT AT LEAST ONE EMAIL ADDRESS OR AN ESTIMATED PATTERN-BASED ADDRESS PER CONTACT",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
